From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:47:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 582/582] Tensor-parallelize the TileLang vision tower and
 aligner across TP ranks

Shard all six ViT and aligner projections (attn.wqkv, attn.wo, mlp.w1,
mlp.w2, aligner.w1, aligner.w2) along output columns (shard_dim = 0) and
all-gather across TP ranks before each consuming projection or residual
add:

- Unconditional by default whenever use_data_parallel is False (no
  SPARK_DS41F_VISION_TP feature flag).
- Every weight and bias shard is a contiguous row range in the
  safetensors checkpoint (rows = 1 in DirectWeightSession.view_records),
  loading directly into model._direct_weight_arena via O_DIRECT without
  strided 2D copy descriptors or bounce buffers.
- Every GEMM and SIMT GEMV accumulates over the full unsharded K
  dimension in FP32 and rounds once to BF16, and tensor_model_parallel_all_gather
  concatenates output columns without floating-point arithmetic, making
  TP1, TP3, and TP4 outputs bit-for-bit identical (_assert_bits).
